ACADEMIC AND PROFESSIONAL WRITING

How do you meet your readers’ needs? Most importantly,
Be “easy” on your readers.

Remember that your job is to make it as easy as possible for your writer to read your writing.
Do this in the following ways:
1) Use direct, clear vocabulary. Use terminology consistently. Do not search for
synonyms or “big” words to replace more concise, clear ones. Use more verbs and
fewer nouns. Be efficient by reducing wordiness and useless language.
Examples:
• The new rod, the purpose of which is to reduce friction, needs to be inserted into the
machine.
The new rod, which reduces friction, must be inserted into the machine.
To reduce friction, insert the new rod into the machine.
• Attempts were made on the part of the research staff with regard to an assessment
of the project.
The engineering staff attempted to assess the project.
• The agency has the responsibility of eliciting, collecting, and distributing grants for
graduate research so that graduate students have an opportunity to earn money by
doing research projects.
The agency solicits, collects, and distributes research grants for graduate student
employment.
• The device was designed to fit under a computer work station, allows a user to do
his normal workday activities such as typing, working on a computer, and talking on
the telephone while at the same time it reduces and even prevents leg cramping that
is caused by sitting in the same position.
• This device fits under a computer work station, allowing a user to type, work on a
computer, and talk on the phone while reducing and even preventing leg cramping
caused by sitting in the same position.

